$ at the point where $t=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345043 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "607c69e9-9d6e-5de2-af4e-cf5bd02dd46c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345043 #edb/ref 1074 "At the point where $t=1$,  the vector ${r}^{′}(1)$ is tangent to the curve.\n\nLet's calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+\\frac{1}{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-\\frac{1}{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨1-\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}},\\,1+\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-1,\\,1+1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=1$  is  $⟨0,\\,2⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345045 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345045 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75199" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345045 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345045 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{-t},\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ at the point where $t=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345045 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d979bdae-e51f-5a47-9ba4-fdf00565f442" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345045 #edb/ref 1074 "At the point where $t=0$,  the vector ${r}^{′}(0)$ is tangent to the curve.\n\nLet's calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{-t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,-{e}^{-t},\\,2t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨{e}^{0},\\,-{e}^{-0},\\,2\\cdot 0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=0$ is $⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400247 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400247 #edb/ref 1069 "q-126841" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400247 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400247 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1),1-5t⟩$ at the point where $t=0,$  valid for all  real values of $u?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400247 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1276b48a-33df-5447-9033-1c8e5ee23a8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400247 #edb/ref 1074 "At the point where $t=0,$ the vector ${r}^{′}(0)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(0)+u{r}^{′}(0),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({0}^{2}+1),1-5(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-5t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+1},-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨\\frac{2(0)}{{0}^{2}+1},-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point where $t=0$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨0,1⟩+u⟨0,-5⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400248 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400248 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400248 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400248 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400248 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400248 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400248 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400248 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186400251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400248 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "19d09d6d-fdd3-564f-8577-1f47d907f393" #edb/ref 1759218604541